  "finding": "After the MC-aware sink fix, v1 and v2 agree EXACTLY on both the number of booked transfers and the moved bytes for every sampled plan (2/2, 10/10, 22/22). The earlier count/byte differences came from ONE cause, not from a per-edge vs per-hop labelling: v2 took `dag.sinks()` on the STATIC graph, so a task whose successors were dropped by the MC realization was not treated as an endpoint and its return was never booked (measured: one 185 B return per graph). The adapter now marks a task as a sink when it is a static sink OR has no surviving successor, matching the v1 engine.",
